 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 646840,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\">\n  <li>The graph that represents <span data-math=\"f(x)=(x+1)^2−4\">f(x)=(x+1)^2−4</span> has its vertex at <span data-math=\"(-1,-4)\">(-1,-4)</span>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Explain how we can tell from the expression <span data-math=\"(x+1)^2−4\">(x+1)^2−4</span> that <span data-math=\"-4\">-4</span> is the minimum value of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> rather than the maximum value.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1273465,
     "content_html": "The coefficient of the quadratic term is positive; therefore, the vertex will be a minimum value."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273466,
     "content_html": "We cannot tell from the expression; we have to graph it."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273467,
     "content_html": "The expression <span data-math=\"(x+1)^2\">(x+1)^2</span> is a squared expression, so its value will always be positive or zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1273468,
     "content_html": "The constant is always the minimum value."
    }
   ],
